+/// What `remap` does with a block of `len` bytes asked to become
+/// `new_len`, when either length is small: true when the class stays,
+/// and the block keeps its place; false when it changes, and the block
+/// must move. For two large lengths, null: only `remap` knows. A List
+/// that doubles, or text that grows by half, always changes class, so
+/// `reallocSlice` judges with this, with no call, before asking.
+pub inline fn smallInPlace(len: usize, new_len: usize, alignment: std.mem.Alignment) ?bool {
+    const new = classOf(new_len, alignment);
+    if (classOf(len, alignment)) |c| return new != null and new.? == c;
+    return if (new != null) false else null;
+}
